          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            If one considers a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperdoctrine"} hyperdoctrine
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+lattices"} subobject lattices
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+contexts"} category of contexts
            and equipped with
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution"} substitution
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context+extension"} context extension
            %em universal closure operator
            or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modality"} modality
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure+operator"} closure operator
            acting on each of the slices and being compatible with the pullback operation. A hyperdoctrine equipped with such an operator is sometimes called a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+hyperdoctrine"} modal hyperdoctrine
          %p
            If there is moreover a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            (hence if that hyperdoctrine is the collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+categories"} slice categories
            of a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            on that subobject classifier,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋄
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Diamond \colon \Omega \to \Omega
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "DefinitionForReflectiveSubcategories"} below
          %p
            Instead of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
            one may consider more generally closures acting on the full
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+categories"} slice categories
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+logic"} modal logic
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type+theory"} modal type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#DefinitionForReflectiveSubcategories For reflective subcategories
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi L
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_j(\mathcal{C}) \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow} \mathcal{E}
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
          %p
            Here we discuss explicit translations between the structure given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} reflector
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            and the corresponding closure operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \colon \Omega \to \Omega
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney operator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type+theory"} modal type theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+%28in+computer+science%29"} monads (in computer science)
            most manifest.
          #ClosureOperatorOfReflection.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Given a reflector
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ♯
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi L
                      %msub
                        %mi Sh
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp : \mathcal{E} \stackrel{L}{\to} Sh_j(\mathcal{E}) \hookrightarrow \mathcal{E}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{E}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %strong closure operator
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset+of+subobjects"} poset of subobjects
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi L
                    %mo :
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    c_L : Sub(X) \to Sub(X)
                    \\,,
            %p
              by sending any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
              classified by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+function"} characteristic function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_A : X \to \Omega
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_L(A)
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c_L(A) &amp;\to&amp; \sharp A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\to&amp; \sharp X
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo ♯
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \sharp X
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} adjunction unit
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              This is well defined. Moreover,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_L
              commutes with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/change+of+base"}> change of base
              ).
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, lemma A4.3.2
            ).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A family of functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(X) \to Sub(X)
              for all objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              that commutes with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/change+of+base"} change of base
              is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %strong universal closure operation
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functor"} left exact
              reflector
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp
              as above with induced closure operation
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_L
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : \Omega \to \Omega
              is given as the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mo ♯
                    %mi Ω
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi χ
                          %mrow
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi true
                    %mi Ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    j : \Omega \to \sharp \Omega \stackrel{\chi_{\sharp true}}{\to} \Omega
                    \\,,
            %p where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo →
                        %mo ♯
                        %mi Ω
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \to \sharp \Omega
                  is the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} adjunction unit
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi χ
                          %mrow
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi true
                        %mo :
                        %mo ♯
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo →
                        %mi Ω
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_{\sharp true} : \sharp \Omega \to \Omega
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+function"} characteristic function
                  of the result of applying
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ♯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp
                  to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} universal subobject
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ↪
                          %mrow
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi true
                        %mo ♯
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mo ♯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ↪
                          %mi true
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (* \stackrel{\sharp true}{\hookrightarrow} \sharp \Omega)
                        \:=
                        \\sharp (* \stackrel{true}{\hookrightarrow} \Omega)
                %p
                  (which is again a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
                  since
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ♯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp
                  preserves
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+function"} characteristic function
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi χ
                        %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_A : X \to \Omega
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi χ
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c_L(A) &amp;\to&amp; &amp;\to&amp; &amp;\to&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\stackrel{\chi_A}{\to}&amp; \Omega
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    \\sharp \Omega
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    \\Omega
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              The pullback along the rightmost morphism is by definition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo #
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mo ♯
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} # * \to \sharp \Omega
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo #
                            %mo *
                            %mo =
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi χ
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c_L(A) &amp;\to&amp; &amp;\to&amp; # * = * &amp;\to&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\stackrel{\chi_A}{\to}&amp; \Omega
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    \\sharp \Omega
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    \\Omega
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Moreover, by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} adjunction unit
              we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi χ
                                    %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ♯
                                  %msub
                                    %mi χ
                                    %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi Ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\to&amp; \sharp X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\chi_A}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\sharp \chi_A}}
                    \\\
                    \\Omega &amp;\to&amp; \sharp \Omega
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p Using this in the remaining bottom morphism of our would-be pullback square we find that equivalently
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo #
                            %mo *
                            %mo =
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo ♯
                                %msub
                                  %mi χ
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c_L(A) &amp;\to&amp; &amp;\to&amp; # * = * &amp;\to&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; \sharp X
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\sharp \chi_A}{\to}&amp;
                    \\sharp \Omega
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    \\Omega
                    }
            %p
              needs to be a pullback diagram. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp
              preserves pullbacks we have that also the middle square in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo #
                            %mo *
                            %mo =
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo ♯
                                %msub
                                  %mi χ
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c_L(A) &amp;\to&amp; \sharp A &amp;\to&amp; # * = * &amp;\to&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; \sharp X
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\sharp \chi_A}{\to}&amp;
                    \\sharp \Omega
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    \\Omega
                    }
            %p
              is a pullback. But then also the left square is a pullback, by def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosureOperatorOfReflection"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Equivalently, by the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : \Omega \to \Omega
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+function"} characteristic function
              of the
              = succeed "-closure," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosureOperatorOfReflection"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * \to \Omega
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+diagram"} pasting diagram
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              squares
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mo *
                            %mo =
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi χ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ♯
                                    %mi true
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c_L(*) &amp;\to&amp; \sharp * = * &amp;\to &amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Omega &amp;\to&amp; \sharp \Omega &amp;\stackrel{\chi_{\sharp true}}{\to} &amp; \Omega
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              In this form the statement appears in the proof of (
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, Theorem A4.3.9
              ).
